{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.RibbonHeckeDimension","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.RibbonHeckeDimension","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.TwistedQuantumDimension","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Linear","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.LinearCombination"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ribbon_hecke_qDim_eq_qint_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ribbon_hecke_qDim_eq_qint_two","kind":"theorem","line":239,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L239-L253","doc":"**`dim_q V = [2]_q`.** Under the hypotheses of `ribbon_hecke_dimension` with `a = q²`,\n`q² ≠ 1` (as `q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0`) and `𝟙_V ≠ 0`, the quantum dimension is `q + q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ribbon_hecke_dimension","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ribbon_hecke_dimension","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L222-L237","doc":"**Hecke skein relation ⟹ `(q − q⁻¹)·dim_q V = a − a⁻¹`.** In a `k`-linear ribbon category, if\n`β_{V,V} − β_{V,V}⁻¹ = (q − q⁻¹)·𝟙`, `θ_V = a·𝟙` and `dim_q V = d·𝟙_{𝟙}`, then\n`((q − q⁻¹)·d)·𝟙_V = (a − a⁻¹)·𝟙_V`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_smul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_smul","kind":"theorem","line":216,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L216-L218","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_sub","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_sub","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L209-L212","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_braiding_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_braiding_inv","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L192-L196","doc":"**Negative curl = inverse twist**: `ptr(β_{V,V}⁻¹) = θ_V⁻¹`. Needs the ribbon axiom. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_eq_ptrInvWith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_eq_ptrInvWith","kind":"theorem","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L187-L190","doc":"The ribbon partial trace rewritten through the inverse closure (`twist_closure_eq`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.twist_closure_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.twist_closure_eq","kind":"theorem","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L160-L185","doc":"**The ribbon evaluation via the inverse braiding**: in a ribbon category\n`(θ ▷ Vᘁ) ≫ β_{V,Vᘁ} ≫ ε = (θ⁻¹ ▷ Vᘁ) ≫ β_{Vᘁ,V}⁻¹ ≫ ε`. Uses the balancing axiom at `(Vᘁ, V)`\nand the ribbon axiom `θ_{Vᘁ} = (θ_V)ᘁ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_id","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_id","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L145-L151","doc":"The ribbon partial trace of `𝟙` is the twisted quantum dimension acting on `X`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_braiding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith_braiding","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L139-L143","doc":"**Positive curl = twist**: `ptr(β_{V,V}) = θ_V`. Holds in any balanced category. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrTwistWith","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L134-L137","doc":"**The ribbon right partial trace**: close the right strand with the ribbon evaluation\n`(θ ▷ Y') ≫ β ≫ ε`, the convention of `qDimTwistedWith`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrInvWith_comp_whiskerLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrInvWith_comp_whiskerLeft","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L124-L127","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrWith_comp_whiskerLeft","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrWith_comp_whiskerLeft","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L119-L122","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrInvWith_whiskerRight_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrInvWith_whiskerRight_comp","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L112-L117","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrWith_whiskerRight_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrWith_whiskerRight_comp","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L105-L110","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrInvWith_braiding_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrInvWith_braiding_inv","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L87-L103","doc":"Mirror image of `ptrWith_braiding`: the inverse-closed partial trace of `β_{V,V}⁻¹` is `𝟙`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrInvWith","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrInvWith","kind":"def","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L83-L85","doc":"**Right partial trace closed with the inverse braiding**: the mirror image of `ptrWith`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ptrWith_braiding","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ptrWith_braiding","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/RibbonHeckeDimension.lean#L64-L81","doc":"**The twistless partial trace of the self-braiding is the identity** in any braided category:\nthe curl of the braided closure `β ≫ ε` cancels the curl of `β_{V,V}`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}